      "body": "# [Diffusion][AMD] Add gfx1250 detection and stop silent CPU fallback for diffusion\r\n\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\n#32754 enables gfx1250 for the SRT path. `multimodal_gen` has its own\r\nplatform-resolution and aiter-gating modules, so it needs the equivalent plumbing before\r\ndiffusion models can be brought up on gfx1250.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n**1. `srt/utils/common.py` — add `is_gfx1250_supported()`**\r\n\r\nAlongside the existing `is_gfx95_supported()` / `is_gfx942_supported()`, same pattern and\r\n`lru_cache`. Note #32754 introduces an identical helper; whichever lands second should drop\r\nits copy. Kept here so this PR is self-contained if it lands first.\r\n\r\n**2. `multimodal_gen/runtime/platforms/aiter.py` — expose `USE_AITER_GFX1250`**\r\n\r\nSo diffusion code can gate arch-specific aiter paths the way it already does for gfx942 and\r\ngfx95x (`USE_AITER_GFX942`, `USE_AITER_GFX95`).\r\n\r\n**3. `multimodal_gen/runtime/platforms/__init__.py` — don't silently fall back to CPU**\r\n\r\nThis is the substantive fix. `rocm_platform_plugin()` decided ROCm-vs-CPU solely on whether\r\n`import amdsmi` and `amdsmi_get_processor_handles()` succeeded:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n    except Exception as e:\r\n        logger.debug(\"ROCm platform is unavailable: %s\", e)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`amdsmi` is an optional dependency and is absent from several ROCm container images. When it\r\nis missing, the exception is swallowed into a `logger.debug` and platform resolution falls\r\nthrough to `CpuPlatform`.\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #32702843322](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/32702843322)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #32702842839](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/32702842839)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 7.2): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #32702843252](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/32702843252)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 3,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "weimin023"
            },
            "body": "Hi @sushildubey171,\r\nI reproduced the same silent CPU fallback on a real AMD gfx1151 / Strix Halo container.\r\n\r\nEnvironment:\r\n\r\n- GPU: Radeon 8060S / gfx1151\r\n- ROCm: 7.2.4\r\n- PyTorch: 2.9.1+rocm7.2.4\r\n- `torch.cuda.is_available()`: `True`\r\n- `torch.version.hip`: available\r\n- `amdsmi`: not installed\r\n\r\nWith the current main branch, automatic diffusion platform detection returns:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nsglang.multimodal_gen.runtime.platforms.cpu.CpuPlatform\r\n```\r\nWhen setting:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSGLANG_DIFFUSION_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=rocm\r\n```\r\nit correctly returns:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsglang.multimodal_gen.runtime.platforms.rocm.RocmPlatform\r\n```\r\nWould it make sense to generalize this PR beyond gfx1250 to cover ROCm/HIP containers without amdsmi, including gfx1151?",
