  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Hi @sushildubey171,\r\nI reproduced the same silent CPU fallback on a real AMD gfx1151 / Strix Halo container.\r\n\r\nEnvironment:\r\n\r\n- GPU: Radeon 8060S / gfx1151\r\n- ROCm: 7.2.4\r\n- PyTorch: 2.9.1+rocm7.2.4\r\n- `torch.cuda.is_available()`: `True`\r\n- `torch.version.hip`: available\r\n- `amdsmi`: not installed\r\n\r\nWith the current main branch, automatic diffusion platform detection returns:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nsglang.multimodal_gen.runtime.platforms.cpu.CpuPlatform\r\n```\r\nWhen setting:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSGLANG_DIFFUSION_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=rocm\r\n```\r\nit correctly returns:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsglang.multimodal_gen.runtime.platforms.rocm.RocmPlatform\r\n```\r\nWould it make sense to generalize this PR beyond gfx1250 to cover ROCm/HIP containers without amdsmi, including gfx1151?",
      "created_at": "2026-09-26T17:44:46Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/35317#issuecomment-5848434525",
      "id": 5848434525,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-26T17:44:46Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "weimin023"
      }
    },
